1:#!/usr/bin/env python3
2:"""#444 DETECTOR: every `hpcmips` subtype the binary advertises in `-H` can
3:actually be CONSTRUCTED, instead of three of eight core-dumping inside
4:`interrupt_handler_lookup()`.
5:
6:Rung 2 (machine construction), and that is the CEILING here rather than a
7:shortcut -- the defect kills the process during `MACHINE_SETUP(hpcmips)`, so
8:a rung-3 cold-debugger probe is not merely unnecessary but impossible: a probe
9:needs a constructed machine and construction is what aborted.
10:
11:WITNESS vs DETECTOR.  The pre-fix witness (`_scratchpad/hpcabort_witness.py`)
12:asserts the SYMPTOM -- 3 of 8 advertised subtypes SIGABRT -- so it correctly
13:goes red once the defect is gone.  This file asserts the REPAIRED property, is
14:red on the pre-fix build, and is built to fail on the mutants listed at the
15:foot of this docstring.  Grading one by the other's clauses is a category error
16:in either direction.
17:
18:THE DEFECT, and every line number below was read out of the file today.
19:`device_add()` copies an `irq=` value VERBATIM into `devinit.interrupt_path`
20:(`src/devices/device.c:336-339`); `DEVINIT(ns16550)` hands that string to
21:`INTERRUPT_CONNECT` (`src/devices/dev_ns16550.c:342`); a name that is neither
22:empty nor a registered path falls out of the scan loop in
23:`src/core/interrupt.c` and reaches :190-198, which prints the failing name,
24:prints every registered path, prints "Aborting." and calls `abort()`.  Three
25:arms of `MACHINE_SETUP(hpcmips)` passed a bare integer where a dotted path
26:belongs -- "0" for the two Casio arms and "17" for the Agenda VR3 -- so those
27:three subtypes could not be started at all.
28:
29:TWO WRONGNESSES, and the detector has to see both.  `dev_vr41xx_init()` is what
30:REGISTERS the `...vrip.N` names (`src/devices/dev_vr41xx.c:691-702`, lines
31:0..25).  The BE-300 and E-105 arms called `device_add` BEFORE it, so correcting
32:only the string would still abort -- at the moment of failure not one `vrip.`
33:name existed.  Rows A3/A4 see that because the run still dies; row S2 sees it
34:in the source ORDER, so the two halves are checked independently.
35:
36:*** THE KNOWN RESIDUAL IS PINNED, NOT HIDDEN -- see row R1. ***  Fixing the
37:abort exposes a SECOND, MILDER defect that the abort used to mask: on the three
38:arms that add a UART of their own, `dev_vr41xx_init()` has ALREADY added an
39:ns16550 of its own (`dev_vr41xx.c:777-787`) with `device_add`'s default
40:`in_use = 1` (`device.c:266`).  Two console inputs then exist, and
41:`console_warn_if_slaves_are_needed()` (`src/console/console.c:994-1007`)
42:exit(1)s unless slave xterms are enabled.  MEASURED: `-x` makes all eight reach
43:the debugger prompt, and `in_use=0` on the machine's own UART does too.  That
44:is a separate fix with a separate judgement behind it (which of the two UARTs
45:is the console on real hardware is not knowable from this tree), so #444 does
46:not make it, and R1 pins the residual as a FAIL-CLOSED ALLOWLIST: the set is
47:derived from the source rather than hardcoded, and EXPECT_X_ONLY must be edited
48:to 0 in the same commit that closes it.
49:
50:WHAT THIS FILE DOES NOT CLAIM.  Nothing about whether a real hpcmips guest
51:boots, and nothing about whether `VRIP_INTR_SIU` is the CORRECT hardware line
52:for these UARTs.  There is no VR41xx datasheet in this tree; the line is a
53:JUDGEMENT and the round records it as one.  Only the path FORM is measured --
54:row C3 shows a registered `vrip.N` being accepted and row C4 shows `vrip.N+1`
55:still aborting, which is what makes acceptance a real lookup rather than a
56:no-op.
57:
58:*** A LINE THAT IS WRONG BUT REGISTERED IS NOT CAUGHT BEHAVIOURALLY BY
59:ANYTHING IN THIS FILE, AND THAT WAS MEASURED. ***  `VRIP_INTR_SIU + 1` is
60:vrip.10, which `dev_vr41xx_init` HAS registered, so it connects in silence and
61:scored 26/26 against every run-based row here.  Row S1 is what closes it, and
62:S1 is a SOURCE-TEXT row -- see its comment for exactly what it does and does
63:not buy.
64:
65:MUTANTS THIS FILE IS BUILT TO KILL (every one built, compiled and MEASURED --
66:see the round record for the scores):
67:  * the pre-fix source                                    -> A3 A4 A5 B1 C5 S1 S2 S3 R1
68:  * only one of the three arms corrected                  -> A3 A4 A5 B1 S1 S2 S3 R1
69:  * the string corrected but `device_add` NOT moved below
70:    `dev_vr41xx_init` on the two Casio arms               -> A3 A4 A5 B1 S2 R1
71:  * `VRIP_INTR_SIU` replaced by an out-of-range line 26   -> A3 A4 A5 B1 C5 S1 R1
72:  * `machine->path` replaced by a hardcoded "machine[0]"  -> C5 ONLY
73:  * `VRIP_INTR_SIU + 1` -- registered, so wired in silence -> S1 ONLY
74:
75:usage:  python3 -u regress/hpcmips_ctor_probe.py [options]
76:        run under WSL (`wsl -d Gentoo`); the binary is a Linux ELF.
77:        --binary PATH   the gxemul to test  (default $GXROOT/build/gxemul)
78:        --source PATH   machine_hpcmips.c for the STATIC rows.  Default: the
79:                        copy in the BINARY's own tree if there is one, else the
80:                        committed source -- the static rows must read the text
81:                        that produced the binary, not some other tree's.
82:        --timeout N     per-run wall budget, seconds (default 40)
83:"""
84:
85:import argparse
86:import os
87:import re
88:import shutil
89:import signal
90:import subprocess
91:import sys
92:import tempfile
93:
94:SIGABRT = int(signal.SIGABRT)          # 6 on Linux
95:
96:HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
97:DEFAULT_ROOT = os.environ.get("GXROOT") or os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(HERE))
98:SEC_SRC = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(HERE), "src", "machines",
99:                       "machine_hpcmips.c")
100:MACHINE = "hpcmips"
101:
102:#  The IDENTITY constant.  A probe copied into a tree where it no longer runs
103:#  all of its rows must not report a green verdict over a shorter file.
104:EXPECT_ROWS = 28
105:
106:#  FAIL-CLOSED ALLOWLIST for the residual described in the docstring: how many
107:#  advertised subtypes still need `-x` because they end up with two console
108:#  inputs.  The MEMBERS are derived from the source (the arms that add a UART of
109:#  their own); this number pins the SIZE so the derivation cannot quietly drift.
110:#  It goes to 0 in the same commit that gives those UARTs `in_use=0` -- or that
111:#  otherwise settles which of the two is the console.
112:EXPECT_X_ONLY = 3
113:
114:#  debugger.c:107.  A debugger command line longer than this is TRUNCATED IN
115:#  SILENCE -- see the comment on rows C3/C4, which is where it bit.
116:MAX_CMD_BUFLEN = 72
117:
118:# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
119:# Result classes.  NOT_RUN is a first-class value and is never "ok": a subtype
120:# whose run never happened must produce a RED row, not a blank.
121:# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
122:OK = "CONSTRUCTED_OK"          # constructed AND reached the debugger prompt
123:LOOKUP = "ABORT_LOOKUP"        # SIGABRT *at interrupt_handler_lookup*
124:XONLY = "NEEDS_XTERM_SLAVES"   # constructed, then exit(1) for two console inputs
125:ABORT_OTHER = "ABORT_OTHER"    # SIGABRT somewhere else entirely
126:SIG_OTHER = "SIGNAL_%d"
127:EXIT_OTHER = "EXIT_%s"
128:TIMEOUT = "TIMEOUT"
129:NOT_RUN = "NOT_RUN"
130:
131:#  Classes in which MACHINE_SETUP itself ran to completion.  XONLY belongs here
132:#  and LOOKUP does not: that is the whole distinction #444 turns on.
133:CONSTRUCTED = (OK, XONLY)
134:
135:_rows = []
136:
137:
138:def row(name, ok, got, want):
139:    _rows.append((name, bool(ok)))
140:    print("  [%s] %-58s got=%s want=%s" % ("ok" if ok else "FAIL", name,
141:                                           got, want))
142:
143:
144:def note(s):
145:    print("  --- %s" % s)
146:
147:
148:# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
149:# Classifier.  A pure function of (returncode, output) so it can be
150:# unit-checked without spawning anything -- see the F rows.
151:# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
152:def classify(rc, out):
153:    if rc is None:
154:        return NOT_RUN
155:    if rc == "timeout":
156:        return TIMEOUT
157:    if rc < 0:
158:        sig = -rc
159:        if sig == SIGABRT:
160:            #  "the process died" and "it died HERE" are different claims.
161:            #  Only the diagnostic makes it the second one.
162:            if "interrupt_handler_lookup(" in out and "Aborting." in out:
163:                return LOOKUP
164:            return ABORT_OTHER
165:        return SIG_OTHER % sig
166:    built = "cpu:" in out and "memory:" in out and "cpu0: starting at" in out
167:    if rc == 1 and built and "More than one console input" in out:
168:        return XONLY
169:    if rc == 0 and built and "GXemul>" in out:
170:        return OK
171:    return EXIT_OTHER % rc
172:
173:
174:def failing_name(out):
175:    m = re.search(r'interrupt_handler_lookup\("([^"]*)"\) failed', out)
176:    return m.group(1) if m else None
177:
178:
179:def available_handlers(out):
180:    """The list the aborting process prints between its header and 'Aborting.'"""
181:    m = re.search(r"Available handler paths are:\n(.*?)\nAborting\.", out, re.S)
182:    if not m:
183:        return None
184:    return [ln.strip() for ln in m.group(1).splitlines() if ln.strip()]
185:
186:
187:# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
188:def _run(argv, tmo, feed=b"quit\n"):
189:    """Returns (rc, out).  rc is an int (negative => killed by that signal),
190:    the string "timeout", or None if the run could not be started at all."""
191:    try:
192:        p = subprocess.run(argv, input=feed, stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
193:                           stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, timeout=tmo)
194:        return p.returncode, p.stdout.decode("utf-8", "replace")
195:    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as e:
196:        return "timeout", (e.stdout or b"").decode("utf-8", "replace")
197:    except OSError as e:
198:        print("  !! could not start %r: %s" % (argv, e))
199:        return None, ""
200:
201:
202:# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
203:# Enumeration.  From the BINARY's own -H, never a hardcoded list: a hardcoded
204:# roster that drifts is exactly the stale-record class this project keeps paying
205:# for.  The parse follows gate 9's awk, gate_asan_sweep.sh:233-249 (OPENED, not
206:# remembered -- an earlier draft cited :50-55, which is prose about the sweep's
207:# cost and not the parser at all): a type line is indented 8 and carries
208:# ("name"); its subtypes are indented 12 and start with "- ".  The alias
209:# character class is that awk's WIDENED one, `[A-Za-z0-9_.+/-]`, for the reason
210:# its own comment at :56-58 records -- the narrow lowercase class silently
211:# re-attributed one machine's subtypes to another.
212:# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
213:def enumerate_subtypes(bin_path, machine, tmo):
214:    rc, text = _run([bin_path, "-H"], tmo, feed=b"")
215:    subs, in_block = [], False
216:    for line in text.splitlines():
217:        mtype = re.match(r'^ {8}\S.*\("([A-Za-z0-9_.+/-]+)"', line)
218:        if mtype:
219:            in_block = (mtype.group(1) == machine)
220:            continue
221:        if in_block:
222:            msub = re.match(r'^ {12}- (.*?)\s*\((.*)\)\s*$', line)
223:            if msub:
224:                aliases = re.findall(r'"([^"]+)"', msub.group(2))
225:                if aliases:
226:                    subs.append((msub.group(1), aliases))
227:    return subs
228:
229:
230:# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
231:# Source scan, bounded to MACHINE_SETUP.  This file switches on
232:# machine->machine_subtype THREE times -- MACHINE_SETUP, MACHINE_DEFAULT_CPU and
233:# MACHINE_DEFAULT_RAM -- and an unbounded scan silently keeps the LAST arm for
234:# each constant, i.e. the RAM table, which holds no device_add and no irq at
235:# all.  Bound it, or the S rows measure nothing.
236:# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
237:def strip_comments(text):
238:    """Blank out /* ... */ bodies, PRESERVING the line count so every number
239:    printed below is still the number in the file.  Doing it per line with a
240:    'starts with *' test was the first draft and it is not closed: a comment
241:    whose continuation line happens to begin with prose reads as code, and the
242:    S rows would then see `VRIP_INTR_SIU` in a sentence ABOUT the constant."""
243:    out, i = [], 0
244:    while True:
245:        j = text.find("/*", i)
246:        if j < 0:
247:            out.append(text[i:])
248:            return "".join(out)
249:        out.append(text[i:j])
250:        k = text.find("*/", j + 2)
251:        if k < 0:
252:            out.append("\n" * text[j:].count("\n"))
253:            return "".join(out)
254:        out.append("\n" * text[j:k].count("\n"))
255:        i = k + 2
256:
257:
258:def scan_source(path):
259:    text = strip_comments(
260:        open(path, "r", encoding="utf-8", errors="replace").read())
261:    lines = text.splitlines()
262:
263:    const_aliases = {}
264:    for m in re.finditer(
265:            r'machine_entry_add_subtype\s*\(\s*me\s*,\s*"([^"]*)"\s*,\s*'
266:            r'(MACHINE_\w+)\s*,\s*((?:"[^"]*"\s*,\s*)+)NULL\s*\)', text, re.S):
267:        const_aliases[m.group(2)] = re.findall(r'"([^"]*)"', m.group(3))
268:
269:    setup_lo = setup_hi = None
270:    for i, ln in enumerate(lines, 1):
271:        if setup_lo is None and re.match(r'^MACHINE_SETUP\(', ln):
272:            setup_lo = i
273:        elif setup_lo is not None and re.match(r'^\}', ln):
274:            setup_hi = i
275:            break
276:    if setup_lo is None or setup_hi is None:
277:        return const_aliases, {}
278:
279:    starts = []
280:    for i, ln in enumerate(lines, 1):
281:        if not (setup_lo <= i <= setup_hi):
282:            continue
283:        m = re.match(r'^\tcase\s+(MACHINE_\w+):', ln)
284:        if m:
285:            starts.append((i, m.group(1)))
286:        elif re.match(r'^\tdefault:', ln):
287:            starts.append((i, None))
288:
289:    arms = {}
290:    for idx, (lno, const) in enumerate(starts):
291:        if const is None:
292:            continue
293:        end = starts[idx + 1][0] if idx + 1 < len(starts) else len(lines) + 1
294:        body = lines[lno - 1:end - 1]
295:        info = {"case_line": lno, "irqs": [], "device_add_lines": [],
296:                "vr41xx_lines": [], "code": "\n".join(body)}
297:        for off, bl in enumerate(body):
298:            n = lno + off
299:            for m in re.finditer(r'irq=([^\s"]*)', bl):
300:                info["irqs"].append((n, m.group(1)))
301:            if "device_add(" in bl:
302:                info["device_add_lines"].append(n)
303:            if "dev_vr41xx_init(" in bl:
304:                info["vr41xx_lines"].append(n)
305:        arms[const] = info
306:    return const_aliases, arms
307:
308:
309:def siu_form(code):
310:    """How an arm spells the VRIP line it hands to device_add.  "plain" is the
311:    constant passed WHOLE as one argument; anything else is named so the S1 row
312:    can say WHICH escape it saw rather than only that one happened."""
313:    if re.search(r'VRIP_INTR_SIU\s*[-+*/]', code) or \
314:       re.search(r'[-+*/]\s*VRIP_INTR_SIU', code):
315:        return "arithmetic"
316:    if re.search(r'VRIP_INTR_SIU\s*[,)]', code):
317:        return "plain"
318:    if "VRIP_INTR_SIU" in code:
319:        return "other-use"
320:    return "absent"
321:
322:
323:#  #444 pass 2: the exact device string each UART-adding arm must hand to
324:#  device_add(), format included.  Written from the source AFTER the fix and
325:#  verified by the row below failing when any character of it moves.  If a future
326:#  round legitimately changes one, change it HERE in the same edit -- that is the
327:#  friction this table exists to create.
328:EXPECT_DEVSTR = {
329:    "be-300": "ns16550 irq=%s.cpu[%i].vrip.%i addr=0x0a008680 addr_mult=4 in_use=%i",
330:    "e-105": "ns16550 irq=%s.cpu[%i].vrip.%i addr=0x0a008680 addr_mult=4 in_use=%i",
331:    "agenda": "ns16550 irq=%s.cpu[%i].vrip.%i addr=0x0c000010",
332:}
333:
334:
335:def device_strings(code):
336:    """Every string literal an arm hands to device_add(), concatenated per call.
337:
338:    #444 pass 2.  S1 pinned one ARGUMENT token and left the FORMAT free, so a
339:    literal written INTO the format -- `vrip.%i` -> `vrip.10` -- kept the
340:    VRIP_INTR_SIU argument in place, read as "plain", and passed.  Four seats
341:    produced that class independently; this returns the whole string so S4 can
342:    pin it instead of one field of it.
343:    """
344:    #  THE LITERAL IS NOT IN THE device_add() CALL.  Every arm builds the string
345:    #  with snprintf(tmpstr, sizeof(tmpstr), "...", ...) and then passes tmpstr,
346:    #  so an extractor reading device_add()'s arguments finds NOTHING -- which is
347:    #  what the first draft of this function did, and the row went red for the
348:    #  wrong reason, reporting empty lists rather than a mismatch.  Read the
349:    #  snprintf that FORMATS the ns16550 string, concatenating its adjacent
350:    #  literals, since C string concatenation splits the format across lines.
351:    out = []
352:    for call in re.findall(r"snprintf\s*\((.*?)\)\s*;", code, re.S):
353:        parts = re.findall(r'"((?:[^"\\]|\\.)*)"', call)
354:        if not parts:
355:            continue
356:        joined = "".join(parts)
357:        if joined.startswith("ns16550"):
358:            out.append(joined)
359:    return out
360:
361:
362:def is_path_like(arg):
363:    """A registered interrupt name is a dotted path ("machine[0].cpu[0].2"),
364:    and every in-tree producer builds it from machine->path with a '.' in it
365:    (dev_vr41xx.c:684, :693, :709).  An argument with no '.' cannot be one --
366:    "0" and a bare "%i" have no dot.  Stated, rather than assumed."""
367:    return "." in arg
368:
369:
370:# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
371:def main():
372:    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()
373:    ap.add_argument("--binary",
374:                    default=os.path.join(DEFAULT_ROOT, "build", "gxemul"))
375:    ap.add_argument("--source", default=None)
376:    ap.add_argument("--timeout", type=int, default=40)
377:    a = ap.parse_args()
378:
379:    binary = os.path.abspath(a.binary)
380:    #  The static rows must read the text that produced THIS binary.  Reading
381:    #  the committed source while testing some other tree's binary is how a
382:    #  green S row gets attributed to a build it never described.
383:    src = a.source
384:    if src is None:
385:        cand = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(binary), "src", "machines",
386:                            "machine_hpcmips.c")
387:        src = cand if os.path.isfile(cand) else SEC_SRC
388:    src = os.path.abspath(src)
389:
390:    print("#444  hpcmips machine construction -- DETECTOR (rung 2)")
391:    print("  binary = %s" % binary)
392:    print("  source = %s" % src)
393:
394:    # ---- instrument -------------------------------------------------------
395:    have = os.path.isfile(binary) and os.access(binary, os.X_OK)
396:    row("P1 binary present and executable", have, have, True)
397:
398:    #  stdbuf: abort() does NOT flush stdio, and stdout to a PIPE is block
399:    #  buffered -- without this the diagnostic is LOST and an aborting run
400:    #  looks like a bare core dump with no evidence of WHERE it died.  Measured
401:    #  on this very defect before the guard existed.  Absent stdbuf must FAIL,
402:    #  never quietly measure nothing.
403:    sb = shutil.which("stdbuf")
404:    row("P2 stdbuf present (abort() does not flush a buffered stdout)",
405:        sb is not None, sb, "a path")
406:
407:    tmp = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="hpcctor.")
408:    raw = os.path.join(tmp, "raw.bin")
409:    try:
410:        with open(raw, "wb") as f:
411:            f.write(b"\0" * 64)
412:        made = os.path.getsize(raw) == 64
413:    except OSError:
414:        made = False
415:    #  A RAW load, not an ELF: the machine constructs, the loader accepts it,
416:    #  the debugger prompt is reached and `quit` gives a clean rc=0.  With a
417:    #  bogus ELF every healthy subtype exits 1 at the loader instead, and then
418:    #  "constructed" and "exit status" stop agreeing.
419:    row("P3 a 64-byte RAW image exists for the loader", made, made, True)
420:
421:    # ---- F rows: the classifier itself, nothing spawned --------------------
422:    row("F1 absent data is not ok (classify(None,'') is NOT_RUN)",
423:        classify(None, "") == NOT_RUN, classify(None, ""), NOT_RUN)
424:    row("F2 rc=0 with no construction evidence is not ok",
425:        classify(0, "") != OK, classify(0, ""), "not " + OK)
426:    row("F3 a SIGABRT WITHOUT the diagnostic is not scored as this defect",
427:        classify(-SIGABRT, "boom") == ABORT_OTHER,
428:        classify(-SIGABRT, "boom"), ABORT_OTHER)
429:    row("F4 a SIGABRT WITH the diagnostic is scored as this defect",
430:        classify(-SIGABRT, 'interrupt_handler_lookup("0") failed.\nAborting.')
431:        == LOOKUP, LOOKUP, LOOKUP)
432:    row("F5 a timeout is not ok",
433:        classify("timeout", "cpu: memory: cpu0: starting at GXemul>")
434:        == TIMEOUT,
435:        classify("timeout", "cpu: memory: cpu0: starting at GXemul>"), TIMEOUT)
436:
437:    if not (have and sb and made):
438:        return finish()
439:    stdbuf = [sb, "-o0", "-e0"]
440:    rawspec = "0x80000000:" + raw
441:
442:    def run_sub(alias, extra=(), feed=b"quit\n"):
443:        argv = list(stdbuf) + [binary, "-V"] + list(extra) + \
444:            ["-E", MACHINE, "-e", alias, rawspec]
445:        return _run(argv, a.timeout, feed)
446:
447:    # ---- enumeration -------------------------------------------------------
448:    subs = enumerate_subtypes(binary, MACHINE, a.timeout)
449:    row("E1 subtypes enumerated from the binary's own -H (not hardcoded)",
450:        len(subs) >= 2, len(subs), ">= 2")
451:    for disp, al in subs:
452:        note("-H says: %-28s %s" % (disp, ", ".join(al)))
453:    if len(subs) < 2:
454:        return finish()
455:
456:    # ---- mode A: default flags ---------------------------------------------
457:    #  Every enumerated subtype starts as NOT_RUN.  Nothing downstream may turn
458:    #  a missing measurement into a pass.
459:    res = {al[0]: [NOT_RUN, ""] for _, al in subs}
460:    print("  RUNS A -- default flags:")
461:    for _disp, al in subs:
462:        rc, out = run_sub(al[0])
463:        res[al[0]] = [classify(rc, out), out]
464:        nm = failing_name(out)
465:        print("    %-14s rc=%-9s %-20s %s"
466:              % (al[0], rc, res[al[0]][0],
467:                 ("name=%r" % nm) if nm is not None else ""))
468:
469:    a_lookup = sorted(k for k, v in res.items() if v[0] == LOOKUP)
470:    a_xonly = sorted(k for k, v in res.items() if v[0] == XONLY)
471:    a_built = sorted(k for k, v in res.items() if v[0] in CONSTRUCTED)
472:    a_other = sorted(k for k, v in res.items() if v[0] not in CONSTRUCTED)
473:
474:    row("A1 every enumerated subtype produced a result (no NOT_RUN)",
475:        all(v[0] != NOT_RUN for v in res.values()),
476:        sum(1 for v in res.values() if v[0] == NOT_RUN), 0)
477:    row("A2 no run hit the wall clock",
478:        all(v[0] != TIMEOUT for v in res.values()),
479:        sum(1 for v in res.values() if v[0] == TIMEOUT), 0)
480:    row("A3 NO subtype dies inside interrupt_handler_lookup",
481:        not a_lookup, "%d aborting %s" % (len(a_lookup), a_lookup),
482:        "0 aborting")
483:    row("A4 every advertised subtype completes MACHINE_SETUP",
484:        len(a_built) == len(subs), "%d/%d" % (len(a_built), len(subs)),
485:        "%d/%d" % (len(subs), len(subs)))
486:    row("A5 no subtype failed in some third, unclassified way",
487:        not a_other, [(k, res[k][0]) for k in a_other], [])
488:
489:    # ---- mode B: with slave xterms enabled ---------------------------------
490:    #  `-x` is an ordinary in-tree flag, not a source edit: it does not change
491:    #  the machine description, the device set or the dispatch.  It is what
492:    #  turns "MACHINE_SETUP finished" into "the emulator is actually usable",
493:    #  which is the property a user cares about.
494:    print("  RUNS B -- with -x (slave xterms allowed):")
495:    bres = {al[0]: NOT_RUN for _, al in subs}
496:    for _disp, al in subs:
497:        rc, out = run_sub(al[0], extra=("-x",))
498:        bres[al[0]] = classify(rc, out)
499:        print("    %-14s rc=%-9s %s" % (al[0], rc, bres[al[0]]))
500:    b_ok = sorted(k for k, v in bres.items() if v == OK)
501:    row("B1 with -x, EVERY advertised subtype reaches the debugger prompt",
502:        len(b_ok) == len(subs), "%d/%d ok, others=%s"
503:        % (len(b_ok), len(subs),
504:           [(k, v) for k, v in sorted(bres.items()) if v != OK]),
505:        "%d/%d" % (len(subs), len(subs)))
506:
507:    # ---- controls ----------------------------------------------------------
508:    rc, out = run_sub("nosuchsubtype")
509:    cls = classify(rc, out)
510:    row("C1 LIVENESS: a bogus subtype is rejected, not scored as constructed",
511:        cls not in CONSTRUCTED and "Unknown subtype" in out, cls,
512:        "rejected, not " + OK)
513:
514:    #  A machine that DOES abort for an unrelated reason (measured:
515:    #  "bus_pci_add(): pci_data == NULL!").  This is the row that stops some
516:    #  future unrelated crash being scored as this defect -- or, worse, this
517:    #  defect's return being scored as something else.
518:    rc, out = _run(list(stdbuf) + [binary, "-V", "-E", "mvmeppc", "-e",
519:                                   "mvme1600", rawspec], a.timeout)
520:    cls = classify(rc, out)
521:    last = ([ln for ln in out.strip().splitlines() if ln.strip()] or [""])[-1]
522:    row("C2 an UNRELATED SIGABRT classifies %s, not %s" % (ABORT_OTHER, LOOKUP),
523:        cls == ABORT_OTHER, "%s (%s)" % (cls, last.strip()[:40]), ABORT_OTHER)
524:
525:    #  C3/C4 -- the DEVICE-SIGNATURE control, and the reason "the path is
526:    #  accepted" is a measurement rather than a tautology.  `device add` in the
527:    #  debugger (debugger_cmds.c:552-553) reaches the SAME device_add ->
528:    #  DEVINIT -> INTERRUPT_CONNECT path the machine setup uses, on a machine
529:    #  that is already constructed.  Feed it a name that cannot exist; the
530:    #  abort prints every registered path, from which the highest vrip line is
531:    #  DERIVED rather than remembered.  Then N must connect and N+1 must not.
532:    #  Both rows are green on the pre-fix binary too: they check the
533:    #  instrument, not the fix.
534:    #
535:    #  *** KEEP EVERY DEBUGGER COMMAND UNDER MAX_CMD_BUFLEN, debugger.c:107.
536:    #  IT IS 72, AND A LONGER LINE IS TRUNCATED IN SILENCE. ***  The first
537:    #  draft of these rows sent 73 and 78 characters; the trailing digits of
538:    #  the path were eaten, so BOTH the accept and the reject arms aborted on
539:    #  "...vrip." and C3 read as a failure of the fix rather than of the probe.
540:    #  The rows caught it only because C4 compares the failing name against the
541:    #  exact string it sent -- which is why it does.
542:    host = (b_ok or a_built or [None])[0]
543:    dev = "device add ns16550 addr=0x0d00%04x irq=%s.cpu[%i].vrip.%s"
544:    maxline, hs = None, []
