1:#!/usr/bin/env python3
2:"""fbpending DRAIN PROBE -- a RUNG-3 detector that MEASURES the pending-interrupt
3:backlog of footbridge timer 1 in ~10 s, instead of waiting 43 s for it to overflow.
4:
5:WHY THIS EXISTS.  The rung-3 witness (fbpending_witness.py) proves the defect by
6:running until the counter wraps, which takes 42.95 s at cats' emulated_hz and cannot
7:be made faster than 31.51 s on ANY machine (the delivery ceiling is
8:TIMER_MAX_CATCHUP x TIMER_BASE_FREQUENCY = 68,157,440 increments per wall second, and
9:timer_tick0 is called from nowhere else).  A gate row cannot spend that.
10:
11:THE TRICK: MEASURE THE COUNTER, DO NOT WAIT FOR IT TO OVERFLOW.
12:
13:  1. The guest arms timer 1 at a KNOWN SLOW rate.  cats' emulated_hz is 50,000,000 and
14:     reload_timer_value() asks for emulated_hz / effective_cycles(load, ctrl, 1).  With
15:     TIMER_FCLK_256 and load 256 that is 50e6 / (256*256) = 762.94 Hz.
16:  2. It free-runs for T seconds.  Nothing acks, so the backlog is rate*T -- UNLESS the
17:     device bounds it.
18:  3. It then FREEZES the timer by writing TIMER_1_LOAD = 0x00FFFFFF while keeping
19:     TIMER_FCLK_256: the rate falls to 50e6/(0xFFFFFF*256) = 0.0116 Hz, one tick per
20:     86 s.  *** A LOAD WRITE DOES NOT CLEAR pending_timer_interrupts *** (only a
21:     TIMER_x_CONTROL write WITHOUT TIMER_ENABLE does, dev_footbridge.c:583), so the
22:     backlog survives the freeze.  That turns a moving quantity into a static one.
23:  4. It then DRAINS AND COUNTS.  DEVICE_TICK writes timer_value = random() %
24:     effective_cycles(load, ctrl, 0) whenever the backlog is > 0, and with load
25:     0x00FFFFFF that modulus is 0xFFFFFF, so the produced value is in [0, 0xFFFFFE].
26:     The guest writes the sentinel 0x00FFFFFF -- which the modulo CANNOT produce and
27:     which survives TIMER_x_VALUE's own `idata & TIMER_MAX_VAL` mask -- and spins.  A
28:     changed read means one tick was delivered; the guest then writes TIMER_1_CLEAR
29:     (one decrement) and repeats.  When the spin budget expires with the sentinel
30:     intact, the backlog is 0 and the number of decrements IS the backlog.
31:
32:  The measured number is the whole verdict: pre-fix it is rate*T.  No wrap, no 43 s,
33:  and the row reports a NUMBER rather than a boolean.
34:
35:  *** POST-FIX IT IS **NOT** THE CAP, AND THE FIRST VERSION OF THIS PARAGRAPH SAID IT
36:  WAS. ***  Measured by a pass-2 seat on ONE binary with ONE bound of 762: backlog 3 at
37:  4 s, 100 at 46 s, 375 at 0.5 s.  Once the bound is first reached the number is a
38:  MODULAR RESIDUE of the delivered tick count, not the bound itself.
39:
40:  That is why `--expect-cap` is a one-sided `bD <= CAP` and CANNOT distinguish a bound
41:  of 762 from one of 7: the quantity it tests is structurally <= the bound whatever the
42:  bound is.  The rows that actually pin the bound's VALUE live in
43:  regress/diff_fbpending_bound.c (R5, an equality against the timer's own rate, and R6,
44:  which re-arms at a different rate) -- and they exist because a one-token mutant
45:  (`freq / 100.0`) destroyed 99% of the guest's clock while passing this probe.
46:
47:ARM X -- THE PLACEMENT DISCRIMINATOR, and the reason it is not merely a second run.
48:  dev_footbridge.c never calls timer_remove() and never lowers the core frequency when
49:  the guest DISABLES a timer: TIMER_x_CONTROL without TIMER_ENABLE zeroes the counter
50:  once (:583) and leaves the struct timer running.  So timer_tickN keeps incrementing a
51:  counter that DEVICE_TICK will never look at.  Arm X arms the timer, immediately
52:  disables it, free-runs, re-enables (which does NOT clear the counter) and then
53:  measures.  A non-zero result proves the counter accrues while the device is disabled
54:  -- which is exactly the state in which a bound placed in DEVICE_TICK cannot run.
55:
56:ARMS
57:  D  enabled throughout.  Backlog after T seconds.
58:  X  disabled during the accrual.  Backlog after T seconds.  Q1's discriminator.
59:  T  negative control: MMU left on, so the footbridge is not mapped.  Must not return
60:     the device's answers.  (machine_cats.c's boot page tables map only the low 256 MB;
61:     the footbridge is at PA 0x42000000.)
62:  K  failability control: arm D's prologue plus ONE instruction, a read of
63:     IRQ_ENABLE_SET, which dev_footbridge.c answers with fatal() then exit(1).  A probe
64:     in which nothing can die proves nothing by surviving.
65:
66:Every RAM output word is poisoned with 0xDEADBEEF first and every verdict row requires
67:the values it consults to be PRESENT.  Every planted instruction is checked, as it
68:EXECUTES, against the emulator's own disassembly (the hand-assembled-encoding trap).
69:
70:usage: fbpending_drain.py <gxemul-binary> <four-byte-raw-stub>
71:                          [--accrue S] [--expect-cap N] [--learn]
72:"""
73:import os, pty, re, select, signal, struct, sys, time
74:
75:BIN = sys.argv[1]
76:STUB = sys.argv[2]
77:LEARN = "--learn" in sys.argv
78:
79:
80:def _opt(name, default, cast):
81:    if name in sys.argv:
82:        return cast(sys.argv[sys.argv.index(name) + 1])
83:    return default
84:
85:
86:ACCRUE_S = _opt("--accrue", 4.0, float)
87:EXPECT_CAP = _opt("--expect-cap", -1, int)   # -1 = report only
88:#  WHICH of the four timers.  dev_footbridge.c derives timer_nr as
89:#  (relative_addr >> 5) & 3, so timer N's registers sit at 0x300 + N*0x20 and
90:#  TIMER_1_* is INDEX 0.  A fix applied to only one of the four callbacks passes a
91:#  row that exercises only timer 1, which is why this is a parameter and not a
92:#  constant.
93:TIMER_NR = _opt("--timer", 0, int)
94:TBASE = 0x300 + 0x20 * TIMER_NR
95:T_LOAD, T_VALUE, T_CTRL, T_CLEAR = TBASE, TBASE + 4, TBASE + 8, TBASE + 12
96:
97:CODE = 0x00008000
98:DATA = 0x00009000
99:FB = 0x42000000
100:
101:EMU_HZ = 50000000.0
102:#  --fast drives the counter at the machine's FULL emulated_hz (load 1, no
103:#  prescaler = 50 MHz on cats), which is the only setting that reaches the 2^31
104:#  wrap inside a run: 2^31 / 50e6 = 42.95 s.  The default 762.94 Hz would need
105:#  32 days.  The freeze/drain machinery below is independent of the accrual rate.
106:FAST = "--fast" in sys.argv
107:LOAD_RUN = 0x001 if FAST else 0x100   # with FCLK_256 -> 50e6/65536 = 762.94 Hz
108:LOAD_FREEZE = 0x00FFFFFF              # with FCLK_256 -> 0.0116 Hz
109:CTRL_ON = 0x80 if FAST else 0x88      # TIMER_ENABLE [| TIMER_FCLK_256]
110:CTRL_OFF = 0x00
111:SENTINEL = 0x00FFFFFF                 # random() % 0xFFFFFF can never produce it
112:SPIN = 0x00010000                     # 65536 iterations ~ 20 device-tick periods
113:LIMIT = 200000
114:RATE = EMU_HZ / (LOAD_RUN * (1.0 if FAST else 256.0))
115:ONLY = _opt("--only", "", str)        # run a single arm, e.g. --only X
116:
117:VENDOR = 0x1011
118:LOADBACK = 0x00345678
119:POISON = 0xDEADBEEF
120:
121:# ---- RAM map (offsets from DATA) -----------------------------------------
122:K_LIVE, K_SRC, K_L, K_FRZ, K_CON, K_SEN, K_SPIN, K_COFF = (
123:    0x00, 0x04, 0x08, 0x0c, 0x10, 0x14, 0x18, 0x1c)
124:O_DRAIN, O_ITER, O_LASTV, O_VEND, O_PHASE, K_LIM = (
125:    0x20, 0x24, 0x28, 0x2c, 0x30, 0x34)
126:
127:CONSTS = {K_LIVE: 0x11223344, K_SRC: 0x12345678, K_L: LOAD_RUN,
128:          K_FRZ: LOAD_FREEZE, K_CON: CTRL_ON, K_SEN: SENTINEL,
129:          K_SPIN: SPIN, K_COFF: CTRL_OFF, K_LIM: LIMIT}
130:OUTS = (O_DRAIN, O_ITER, O_LASTV, O_VEND, O_PHASE)
131:
132:R = dict(r0=0, r1=1, r2=2, r3=3, r4=4, r5=5, r6=6, r7=7, r8=8, r9=9,
133:         sl=10, fp=11, ip=12, sp=13, lr=14, pc=15)
134:
135:
136:# ---------------------------------------------------------------- assembler
137:#  Encodings are GENERATED, not typed.  Every generated word is still checked
138:#  against the emulator's own disassembly as it executes (arm E of the witness
139:#  found this class of error four times in this project).
140:def _imm12(v):
141:    for rot in range(16):
142:        c = ((v << (2 * rot)) | (v >> (32 - 2 * rot))) & 0xFFFFFFFF
143:        if c < 256:
144:            return (rot << 8) | c
145:    raise ValueError("0x%x is not an ARM immediate" % v)
146:
147:
148:def mov(rd, imm):
149:    return 0xE3A00000 | (R[rd] << 12) | _imm12(imm), "mov %s,#0x%x" % (rd, imm)
150:
151:
152:def movr(rd, rm):
153:    return 0xE1A00000 | (R[rd] << 12) | R[rm], "mov %s,%s" % (rd, rm)
154:
155:
156:def ldr(rd, rn, off):
157:    return 0xE5900000 | (R[rn] << 16) | (R[rd] << 12) | off, \
158:        "ldr %s,[%s,#%d]" % (rd, rn, off)
159:
160:
161:def st(rd, rn, off):
162:    return 0xE5800000 | (R[rn] << 16) | (R[rd] << 12) | off, \
163:        "str %s,[%s,#%d]" % (rd, rn, off)
164:
165:
166:def cmpr(rn, rm):
167:    return 0xE1500000 | (R[rn] << 16) | R[rm], "cmps %s,%s" % (rn, rm)
168:
169:
170:def subs1(rd):
171:    return 0xE2500001 | (R[rd] << 16) | (R[rd] << 12), "subs %s,%s,#1" % (rd, rd)
172:
173:
174:def add1(rd):
175:    return 0xE2800001 | (R[rd] << 16) | (R[rd] << 12), "add %s,%s,#1" % (rd, rd)
176:
177:
178:def br(cond, target, here):
179:    off = ((target - here - 8) >> 2) & 0xFFFFFF
180:    return (cond << 28) | 0x0A000000 | off, None
181:
182:
183:NOP = (0xE1A00000, "mov r0,r0")
184:
185:
186:def build(mmu_on=False, disable_during_accrual=False, kill=False):
187:    """Returns [(offset, word, expected_disassembly_or_None, comment)]."""
188:    p = []
189:
190:    def emit(off, wt, comment=""):
191:        p.append((off, wt[0], wt[1], comment))
192:
193:    if mmu_on:
194:        for o in (0x00, 0x04, 0x08):
195:            emit(o, NOP, "arm T: MMU LEFT ON -- the negative control")
196:    else:
197:        p.append((0x00, 0xEE110F10, "mrc 15,0,r0,cr1,cr0,0", "read CP15 c1"))
198:        p.append((0x04, 0xE3C00001, "bic r0,r0,#1", "clear MMU enable"))
199:        p.append((0x08, 0xEE010F10, "mcr 15,0,r0,cr1,cr0,0", "MMU OFF -> VA == PA"))
200:    p.append((0x0c, 0xEE113F10, "mrc 15,0,r3,cr1,cr0,0", "C2: CP15 c1 read BACK"))
201:    emit(0x10, mov("r0", FB), "footbridge base")
202:    emit(0x14, mov("r4", DATA), "scratch RAM")
203:    emit(0x18, ldr("r5", "r4", K_LIVE), "C1 liveness, expect 0x11223344")
204:    emit(0x1c, ldr("r6", "r0", 0), "A1 VENDOR_ID, expect 0x1011")
205:    emit(0x20, ldr("r2", "r4", K_SRC), "0x12345678 out of RAM")
206:    emit(0x24, st("r2", "r0", T_LOAD), "TIMER_x_LOAD <- 0x12345678")
207:    emit(0x28, ldr("r7", "r0", T_LOAD), "A2 expect 0x00345678 (the handler's mask)")
208:    emit(0x2c, ldr("r2", "r4", K_CON), "CTRL = TIMER_ENABLE|TIMER_FCLK_256")
209:    emit(0x30, st("r2", "r0", T_CTRL), "TIMER_1_CONTROL <- 0x88")
210:    emit(0x34, ldr("r2", "r4", K_L), "load 256")
211:    emit(0x38, st("r2", "r0", T_LOAD), "TIMER_1_LOAD <- 256 => 762.94 Hz")
212:    emit(0x3c, ldr("r8", "r4", K_SEN), "sentinel 0x00FFFFFF")
213:    emit(0x40, ldr("ip", "r4", K_SPIN), "spin budget")
214:    emit(0x44, mov("sl", 0), "drained count")
215:    emit(0x48, mov("lr", 0), "accrual iterations")
216:    emit(0x4c, mov("r1", 0), "")
217:    emit(0x50, st("r1", "r4", O_PHASE), "PHASE = 0")
218:    if disable_during_accrual:
219:        emit(0x54, ldr("r2", "r4", K_COFF), "arm X: CTRL = 0")
220:        emit(0x58, st("r2", "r0", T_CTRL),
221:             "arm X: DISABLE.  Zeroes the counter ONCE and leaves the core timer running.")
222:    else:
223:        emit(0x54, NOP, "")
224:        emit(0x58, NOP, "")
225:    if kill:
226:        p.append((0x5c, 0xE5907188, "ldr r7,[r0,#392]",
227:                  "arm K: IRQ_ENABLE_SET -> fatal()+exit(1)"))
228:        emit(0x60, NOP, "")
229:        return p
230:    #  accrual loop -- publishes liveness and a fresh VENDOR_ID every iteration
231:    emit(0x5c, add1("lr"), "ACCRUE: iterations++")
232:    emit(0x60, st("lr", "r4", O_ITER), "publish iterations")
233:    emit(0x64, ldr("r1", "r0", 0), "fresh VENDOR_ID read, every iteration")
234:    emit(0x68, st("r1", "r4", O_VEND), "publish it")
235:    p.append((0x6c, br(0xE, CODE + 0x5c, CODE + 0x6c)[0], None, "b ACCRUE"))
236:    #  ---- DRAIN entry.  The harness sets pc here after the accrual free-run. ----
237:    if disable_during_accrual:
238:        emit(0x70, ldr("r2", "r4", K_CON), "arm X: re-enable")
239:        emit(0x74, st("r2", "r0", T_CTRL),
240:             "arm X: CONTROL <- 0x88.  reload_timer_value() does NOT clear the counter.")
241:    else:
242:        emit(0x70, NOP, "")
243:        emit(0x74, NOP, "")
244:    emit(0x78, ldr("r2", "r4", K_FRZ), "0x00FFFFFF")
245:    emit(0x7c, st("r2", "r0", T_LOAD), "FREEZE: LOAD <- 0x00FFFFFF => 0.0116 Hz")
246:    emit(0x80, mov("r1", 1), "")
247:    emit(0x84, st("r1", "r4", O_PHASE), "PHASE = 1")
248:    emit(0x88, ldr("sp", "r4", K_LIM), "drain limit")
249:    emit(0x8c, st("r8", "r0", T_VALUE), "DLOOP: TIMER_1_VALUE <- sentinel")
250:    emit(0x90, movr("fp", "ip"), "reset spin budget")
251:    emit(0x94, ldr("r9", "r0", T_VALUE), "SPIN: read TIMER_1_VALUE")
252:    emit(0x98, cmpr("r9", "r8"), "")
253:    p.append((0x9c, br(0x1, CODE + 0xac, CODE + 0x9c)[0], None, "bne TICKSEEN"))
254:    emit(0xa0, subs1("fp"), "")
255:    p.append((0xa4, br(0x1, CODE + 0x94, CODE + 0xa4)[0], None, "bne SPIN"))
256:    p.append((0xa8, br(0xE, CODE + 0xc8, CODE + 0xa8)[0], None,
257:              "budget expired, sentinel intact -> backlog is 0"))
258:    emit(0xac, st("r9", "r4", O_LASTV), "TICKSEEN: publish the value the tick wrote")
259:    emit(0xb0, st("r1", "r0", T_CLEAR), "TIMER_1_CLEAR -- one decrement")
260:    emit(0xb4, add1("sl"), "")
261:    emit(0xb8, st("sl", "r4", O_DRAIN), "publish the drained count")
262:    emit(0xbc, cmpr("sl", "sp"), "")
263:    p.append((0xc0, br(0xA, CODE + 0xdc, CODE + 0xc0)[0], None, "bge OVER"))
264:    p.append((0xc4, br(0xE, CODE + 0x8c, CODE + 0xc4)[0], None, "b DLOOP"))
265:    emit(0xc8, mov("r1", 3), "DONE:")
266:    emit(0xcc, st("r1", "r4", O_PHASE), "PHASE = 3")
267:    emit(0xd0, ldr("r1", "r0", 0), "final VENDOR_ID")
268:    emit(0xd4, st("r1", "r4", O_VEND), "")
269:    p.append((0xd8, br(0xE, CODE + 0xd8, CODE + 0xd8)[0], None, "HALT"))
270:    emit(0xdc, mov("r1", 4), "OVER:")
271:    emit(0xe0, st("r1", "r4", O_PHASE), "PHASE = 4 -- drain limit hit")
272:    p.append((0xe4, br(0xE, CODE + 0xd8, CODE + 0xe4)[0], None, "b HALT"))
273:    return p
