The hpcmips probe currently pins **28 rows**; the manifest’s introductory count is stale. Its new row needs the ordinary HEAD binary and must run before the ASan-build check, which exits the whole gate when that optional build is absent.

For fbpending, the sketch will require an explicit cap and an exact `FBDRAIN_VERDICT=PASS`. Exit zero alone would accept report-only mode. A synchronous run after the LUNA section appears to leave its per-run accounting intact; I’m checking the remaining limits before naming the mutant control.
