76:
77:  CATCHES: edits to the write-arm phase guard that let host stores reach the ring
78:    during DATA-IN.
79:      * dropping the phase conjunct, or re-aiming it at another phase -- measured,
80:        17 of 20, via the post-re-arm readback returning injected bytes;
