1483:#  A python interpreter token.  Bare python/python3, or the $PY-style indirections other
1484:#  harnesses in this tree use.  Anchored so python3.12 and mypython do not match.
1485:#  *** THE TRAILING BOUNDARY IS LOAD-BEARING AND THE FIRST VERSION LACKED IT. ***  A
1486:#  flagship review MEASURED that `"$PYLINT" probe.py` scored as WIRING: the alternation
1487:#  had no boundary after the group, so ANY $PY-prefixed variable read as an interpreter
1488:#  and a linter invocation would have marked a probe wired.  That is the FALSE ACCEPT
1489:#  direction -- the one that silently stops demanding a gate.  Latent rather than live:
1490:#  no such variable exists in the battery today.  `$PYTHON` and `$PY` still match;
1491:#  `$PYLINT` and `$PYTEST` no longer do.
