CODEX_WIRINGCLIFF_PLAN_20260910

The two wirings can be sketched concretely, but they are not yet verified, and two wirings plus four re-dates do not close the separate `fbpending_bound` deadline. This review ran only Git, text, and AST derivations; no gates, builds, probes, or edits.

1. **The six exemptions and the two-versus-four exit-status split still hold.**

   HEAD is `1ce8296`. I repeated the date grep, `sys.exit` search, terminal-file reads, and AST counts, and compared the named files against `b4d4177`. The six probes and named gates/helpers are unchanged. The manifest changed by **55 insertions and one deletion**, but its `EXEMPT` dictionary is unchanged.

   All six entries still expire **after September 20**: `d < today` is false on September 20 and true on **September 21**. The pre-commit consumer still treats checker failure as failure. Anchors: `EXEMPT`, `d < today` in [check_probe_wiring.py](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py:1403); `PWCHK=` in [precommit_check.sh](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/tools/precommit_check.sh:513).

   | Probe | Current completed-measurement exit behavior |
   |---|---|
   | [fbpending_drain_probe.py](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/fbpending_drain_probe.py:715) | Enforceable with a cap: `sys.exit(0 if good else 1)`. Otherwise `sys.exit(0 if ok else 1)` grades controls and can report `REPORT-ONLY`. |
   | [hpcmips_ctor_probe.py](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/hpcmips_ctor_probe.py:746) | `sys.exit(main())`; `finish()` returns `1 if fails else 0`. |
   | [wdc_altoffset_probe.py](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/wdc_altoffset_probe.py:682) | Computes `ok`, writes results, then bare `main()` returns normally. |
   | [wdc_altoffset_sig_probe.py](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/wdc_altoffset_sig_probe.py:246) | Prints classifications and writes `TABLE_C.txt`; no measurement-dependent exit. |
   | [wdc_altoffset_4bit_probe.py](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/wdc_altoffset_4bit_probe.py:222) | Prints classifications and writes `TABLE_4BIT.txt`; no measurement-dependent exit. |
   | [wdc_addtoinbuf_probe.py](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/wdc_addtoinbuf_probe.py:824) | Counts failed predictions, prints completion, then returns normally. |

   Thus “always zero” needs the existing qualification: **measurement failures do not control these four exits; uncaught apparatus exceptions can still exit nonzero.** Also, fbpending’s two expressions use `good` and `ok`, not `ok` twice.

   Other source-derived figures still hold: main altoffset has **18 rows / 36 predictions**, **18 distinct registers**, maximum label width **53**, and **four** differing rows (`s4`, `s5`, `t5`, `t6`); addtoinbuf has **15 rows / 30 predictions**. `GATES=(` in [run.sh](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/run.sh:10) still names **16 gates**, and `gate_wdc.sh` remains absent. Current hpcmips has **28 row calls**, agreeing with `EXPECT_ROWS = 28`; the manifest’s introductory historical counts are unsuitable as its gate denominator.

2. **hpcmips belongs immediately after `gate_begin`, before the ASan-build skip.**

   The anchor `[ -x "$ASAN_HEAD" ] || gate_skip` in [gate_asan_sweep.sh](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/gate_asan_sweep.sh:97) guards availability of the optional `/tmp/gx-asan-head/gxemul` build. It exits the entire script. Placing the ordinary-binary construction probe below it would unnecessarily make its coverage depend on that build.

   Hoist the existing `ulimit -c 0` there too: this probe deliberately exercises aborting controls.

   ```bash
   # SKETCH: after gate_begin, before the ASAN_HEAD availability check.
   ulimit -c 0 2>/dev/null || true

   HPCLOG=$LOGDIR/gate_hpcmips_ctor.log
   hpc_rc=0
   python3 -u "$HERE/hpcmips_ctor_probe.py" \
       --binary "$ROOT/build/gxemul" \
       --source "$HERE/../src/machines/machine_hpcmips.c" \
